WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.829
The Boot.

00:00:00.829 --> 00:00:04.352
How institutional power crushes accountability in Canada.

00:00:04.352 --> 00:00:06.193
Twelve documented cases.

00:00:06.193 --> 00:00:08.340
Zero retaliators prosecuted.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.045
That is not a failure rate.

00:00:10.045 --> 00:00:11.409
That is a policy.

00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:13.443
Vice-Admiral Mark Norman.

00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:17.988
Prosecuted in 2017 for allegedly leaking cabinet confidence.

00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:19.818
The Crown withheld documents.

00:00:19.818 --> 00:00:22.318
The case was stayed in 2019.

00:00:22.318 --> 00:00:25.159
No one was held accountable for the wrongful prosecution.

00:00:25.159 --> 00:00:29.738
The system worked exactly as designed — it punished the person who told the truth.

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:34.420
Three journalists have been criminally prosecuted in Canada for receiving leaked documents.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.932
Not for the wrongdoing those documents exposed.

00:00:36.932 --> 00:00:38.170
For receiving them.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:43.022
The message is clear: if you report government misconduct, you will be the one investigated.

00:00:43.022 --> 00:00:49.670
Sean Bruyea — a veterans' advocate — had his private medical records shared across Veterans Affairs without consent.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.897
Five hundred and thirty-four thousand dollars in settlement.

00:00:52.897 --> 00:00:54.545
No official disciplined.

00:00:54.545 --> 00:00:56.204
No criminal charges.

00:00:56.204 --> 00:00:57.784
Access to Information.

00:00:57.784 --> 00:00:59.999
The legal deadline is thirty days.

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:03.454
The average response time exceeds one hundred and ninety days.

00:01:03.454 --> 00:01:07.124
Thirty to forty percent of requests produce zero documents.

00:01:07.124 --> 00:01:08.738
The system is not broken.

00:01:08.738 --> 00:01:10.579
It is performing as intended.

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:14.613
Prorogation has been used three times to kill parliamentary inquiries.

00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:17.011
2008. 2009.

00:01:17.011 --> 00:01:21.568
2020. Each time, active investigations were terminated overnight.

00:01:21.568 --> 00:01:25.056
Constitutional power weaponized against accountability.

00:01:25.056 --> 00:01:29.749
The Criminal Code contains every tool needed to prosecute institutional retaliation.

00:01:29.749 --> 00:01:32.465
Breach of trust under Section 122.

00:01:32.465 --> 00:01:35.523
Obstruction of justice under Section 139.

00:01:35.523 --> 00:01:36.874
The tools exist.

00:01:36.874 --> 00:01:38.590
The will to use them does not.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.681
Every case documented here follows the same structure.

00:01:41.681 --> 00:01:44.909
A person with evidence of wrongdoing tries to expose it.

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:48.829
The institution redirects all resources toward destroying that person.

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:51.056
The wrongdoing continues unchecked.

00:01:51.056 --> 00:01:54.488
The pattern spans thirty years and multiple governments.
